{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "SNG",
  "chapter": 2,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.2.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the rose of Sharon, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the lily of the valleys.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.2.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As the lily among thorns, so ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my love among the daughters.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.2.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As the apple-tree among the trees of the wood, so ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my beloved among the sons. I sat down under his shadow with great delight, and his fruit ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " sweet to my taste.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.2.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He brought me to the banqueting house, and his banner over me ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " love.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.2.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Stay me with flagons, comfort me with apples: for I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " sick with love.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.2.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His left hand ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " under my head, and his right hand doth embrace me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.2.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I charge you, O ye daughters of Jerusalem, by the roes, and by the hinds of the field, that ye stir not, nor awake ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " love, till he please.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.2.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The voice of my beloved! behold, he cometh leaping upon the mountains, skipping upon the hills.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.2.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My beloved is like a roe, or a young hart: behold, he standeth behind our wall, he looketh forth at the windows, showing himself through the lattice.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.2.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My beloved spoke, and said to me, Rise, my love, my fair one, and come away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.2.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For lo, the winter is past, the rain is over ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " gone.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.2.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The flowers appear on the earth; the time of the singing ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of birds",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " is come, and the voice of the turtle is heard in our land;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.2.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The fig-tree putteth forth her green figs, and the vines ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "with",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the tender grape give a ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "good",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " smell. Arise, my love, my fair one, and come away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.2.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O my dove, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the clefts of the rock, in the secret ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "places",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of the stairs, let me see thy countenance, let me hear thy voice; for sweet ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy voice, and thy countenance ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " comely.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.2.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Take for us the foxes, the little foxes, that spoil the vines: for our vines ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "have",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " tender grapes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.2.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My beloved ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mine, and I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his: he feedeth among the lilies.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.2.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Until the day shall break, and the shadows flee away, turn, my beloved, and be thou like a roe or a young hart upon the mountains of Bether.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
